      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure! A diesel turbocharger uses the exhaust gases to spin a turbine. This turbine connects to a compressor, which compresses the incoming air and forces it into the engine’s intake. When the turbocharger spins faster than the engine, it creates a vacuum that draws more air into the engine, increasing the engine's power output. The exhaust gas drives a turbine that powers this compressor, utilizing the energy in the exhaust to optimize engine performance.",
